description:
Create a config system for taxonomy, thresholds, and prompt templates:

```typescript
const config = {
  taxonomy: {
    work: { areas: ['projects', 'admin', 'learning', 'meetings', 'ideas'] },
    personal: { areas: ['family', 'health', 'finance', 'home', 'hobbies', 'ideas'] }
  },
  thresholds: {
    filed: 0.8,      // High confidence - file directly
    flagged: 0.5,    // Medium - file but flag for review
    clarification: 0.5  // Below this - ask for clarification
  },
  prompts: {
    classifier: '...',
    taskExtractor: '...',
    projectExtractor: '...',
    ideaExtractor: '...',
    clarificationGenerator: '...'
  }
};
```

Files:
- /packages/config/taxonomy.ts
- /packages/config/thresholds.ts
- /packages/config/prompts/classifier.ts
- /packages/config/prompts/extractors.ts
- /packages/config/index.ts

Config should be easily modifiable without code changes.

Create an LLM abstraction layer so providers can be swapped:

```typescript
interface LLMProvider {
  classify(text: string, context?: PersonalContext[]): Promise<ClassificationResult>;
  extract(text: string, type: ItemType, context?: PersonalContext[]): Promise<ExtractionResult>;
  generateClarification(text: string): Promise<ClarificationQuestion>;
  interpretCorrection(original: any, correction: string): Promise<CorrectionResult>;
}
```

Files:
- /packages/api/src/llm/provider.ts (interface)
- /packages/api/src/llm/claude.ts (Claude implementation)
- /packages/api/src/llm/types.ts (result types)

Use @anthropic-ai/sdk. Provider should be injectable/configurable.
